[20:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'After strength testing, we reinforced'

[20:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the connections. New parts were added, angled so they don\'t interfere with a smooth connection. They only make contact when the unit is lifted. The original two legs already act as a stopper, so it won\'t move any further.'

[20:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To kill any wiggle, we added fins just.3 mm taller than needed to keep the connection tight. &gt;&gt; Runners also needed to ditch springs to'

[21:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'slide effortlessly, but we wanted to keep them inserting from the front of the module. This is what we came up with. A stopper is inserted from the side. It\'s a little skewed to act like it\'s spring-loaded after you push it in.'

[21:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This stops it from falling out, even after getting hit. But you might have noticed we have some variants that only have access from one side. How do we insert those stoppers after trapping the box inside? Here\'s what we came up with.'

[21:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Two thin panels with stoppers thick enough to work, but thin enough to slide in. Plus a gasket insert to stop them from falling out.'

[21:44] [scene:talk]
